## 🔐 Platform Credential Setup

Configure API credentials for each platform before running the application.

<details>
<summary><b>📱 Telegram</b> (Click to expand)</summary>

1. Open Telegram and search for **@BotFather**.
2. Send `/newbot` and follow the instructions.
3. Copy the generated bot token.
4. Add your bot as an administrator to the target channel.
5. Get the channel ID:

```bash
curl "https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates"
```

6. Add credentials to `.env`:

```env
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=your_telegram_bot_token
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=-1001234567890
```

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>🎮 Discord</b> (Click to expand)</summary>

1. Open Discord Server Settings.
2. Go to **Integrations → Webhooks → New Webhook**.
3. Select a channel and copy the Webhook URL.
4. Add to `.env`:

```env
DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=https://discord.com/api/webhooks/your_id/your_token
```

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>💬 Slack</b> (Click to expand)</summary>

1. Create an app at [Slack API](https://api.slack.com/apps).
2. Navigate to **OAuth & Permissions**.
3. Add the `chat:write` Bot Token Scope.
4. Install the app in your workspace.
5. Copy the Bot User OAuth Token (`xoxb-...`).
6. Invite the bot to your target channel:

```text
/invite @YourBot
```

7. Add to `.env`:

```env
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-your-slack-bot-token
SLACK_CHANNEL=#your-channel-name
```

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>💼 LinkedIn</b> (Click to expand)</summary>

1. Create an app at [LinkedIn Developer Portal](https://www.linkedin.com/developers/apps).
2. Request the `w_member_social` permission.
3. Complete the OAuth 2.0 flow.
4. Obtain your access token and Person URN.
5. Add to `.env`:

```env
LINKEDIN_ACCESS_TOKEN=your_linkedin_access_token
LINKEDIN_PERSON_URN=urn:li:person:your_person_id
```

**Note:** LinkedIn may return `403 ACCESS_DENIED` if the required permissions or API access have not been approved. This demonstrates platform-specific error handling.

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>🚀 DEV Community (DEV.to)</b> (Click to expand)</summary>

1. Log in to [DEV Community](https://dev.to/).
2. Navigate to **Settings → Extensions**.
3. Generate a DEV Community API Key.
4. Add to `.env`:

```env
DEVTO_API_KEY=your_devto_api_key
```

</details>
